course: dictionary
lesson: 3513
title: Fatigue: more than feeling sleepy
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: Fatigue means great tiredness, the kind you feel after hard work, illness or lack of sleep. Look at the clues around it: «After three hours of looking at paintings, the family felt fatigue in their feet and eyes.» Hours of looking and tired feet and eyes tell you fatigue means very worn out.
explain: Picture Dad at the Louvre saying, «We'll see the whole lot before lunch, easy.» The word easy is a clue that he is joking a little. Nobody can see everything in one day, so he is exaggerating. Tired legs and eyes from too much looking have a name: museum fatigue.
explain: Fatigue can also mean weakness in metal, so context matters. «The bridge's steel had metal fatigue after years of being shaken by heavy lorries.» Shaking and bending are the clues here, so the word means weakness in metal, not tiredness. Always check which meaning fits the sentence.
fact: Fatigue means great tiredness of the body or mind.
fact: Fatigue can come after hard work, illness or lack of sleep.
fact: Metal fatigue is weakness in metal caused by being bent or shaken many times, which can make it crack.
fact: Fatigues, in the plural, are loose army clothes for work or battle.
fact: Phrases you may meet include «battle fatigue», «news fatigue» and «museum fatigue».
exercise: «After a long day of hard training, Maya felt fatigue in every muscle.» What does fatigue mean here? | A new pair of trainers | A loud noise | *Great tiredness | Wet and cold
exercise: «The bridge's steel had metal fatigue after years of being shaken by heavy lorries.» What is metal fatigue? | Shiny paint on metal | Metal that floats on water | Metal that is too hot to touch | *Weakness in metal caused by being bent or shaken many times
exercise: «The soldiers wore green fatigues on the training ground.» What are fatigues? | Tiny flowers | *Loose army clothes for work or battle | Very fast cars | Long, sharp swords
test: Museum fatigue is the name for tired legs and eyes after too much looking. What causes museum fatigue? | Sleeping in the museum | Eating too many snacks | *Looking at far more than anyone can see in one day | Reading only one book
test: «The long, noisy journey will fatigue the whole class.» What does fatigue mean in this sentence? | To mend something | *To make someone very tired | To feel cold | To shout loudly
exam: «Battle fatigue» is an old name for a mental injury from combat. What does battle fatigue mean? | A shiny metal part of a tank | *An old name for a mental injury soldiers get from combat, now called trauma | A tired soldier's breakfast | A kind of army dance
